<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output down 6% yr/yr in August.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output down 6% yr/yr in August.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    Aug 96     July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   81.5	 83.3	     86.6</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months  </p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) Aug 96     July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> industry as a whole		 93.9	 94.4	  94.5</p>
<p> industry ex construction	  98.8	 99.2	  97.0</p>
<p> construction industry	     75.2	 76.0	  84.8</p>
<p> intermediate goods		  93.3	 93.5	  95.8</p>
<p> consumer non-durables	    102.8	103.3	  98.5</p>
<p> consumer durables		   98.6	 98.5	  99.6</p>
<p> investment goods		    99.6	101.2	  98.4</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710 86.6</p>
